<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame">
      <h2>The Co-Founders</h2>
      <p class="lede">Edward Gregory &amp; Jim Rankin</p>
      <p>Edward is a natural philosopher in the old, unembarrassed sense of the phrase: someone who refuses to
      choose between the telescope and the tree. He co-founded EGregoRA to build the thing he could never find —
      a place where cosmology, ecology, neuroscience and the esoteric traditions could be argued about in the
      same room, by the same person, without anyone having to pretend.</p>
      <p><strong>Jim Rankin</strong> is co-founder of the order — Ed's understudy, and on the better days his
      muse. Where Ed presses a question until it yields, Jim is the one who asks why that question and not
      another; a good deal of what EGregoRA now calls its own began as something Jim said sideways and Ed
      refused to let go of. The two halves of the work, the pursuit and the provocation.</p>
      <p>Their standing instruction to every member is three words long: <em>test everything kindly</em>.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/ask-ed/">Put a question to Ed</a></p>
    </div>
